    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="letterhead"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__115"
                            type="person">H. W. Baerensprung</rs>
                        <lb/>243 Riverside Dr. <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place"
                            >New York</rs> 25, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N.
                            Y.</rs></fw><dateline><date when="1946-05-22">May 22nd,
                        1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Mr. Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>Not so long ago I told you that I had received three requests to return to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> in order to
                    participate in the reconstruction of <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122"
                        type="place">Germany</rs>.</p>
                <p>The requests to return came from <lb/>a) <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3492"
                        type="person">Mr. Hans Venedey</rs>, Minister of the Interior of Greater
                        <sic>Hesse</sic>, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__471" type="place"
                        >Wiesbaden</rs>. (encl. A) <lb/>b) <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3493"
                        type="person">Mr. Hans Menzel</rs>, President of the Bavarian Labor Office,
                        <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__306" type="place">Munich</rs>. (encl. B) <lb/>c)
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3494" type="person">Mr. Amelunxen</rs>,
                        <q>Oberpräsident</q> of Westphalia, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__307"
                        type="place">Münster i. W.</rs> (encl. C) </p>
                <p>The enclosures which I attach are copies of the written requests; they are
                    self-explanatory. Furthermore I am sending you my curriculum vitae (encl. D) and
                    also a note on my friend <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3495" type="person">Erich
                        Lewinski</rs> who likewise wishes to return to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs>. I am sending you
                    this material because I would like you to advise me on how to proceed to
                    expedite our return. So far, I have not heard from any U. S. authority in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__554" type="place">Washington, D. C.</rs> except a
                    note from the State Department dated <date when="1946-02-28">February 28th,
                        1946</date> that my application for permission to depart from the <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__684" type="place">USA</rs> had been received and had
                    been assigned Application Nr. 23o84.<!-- <q>o</q> über <q>)</q> --> The State
                    Department has complete files about me since from 1943 – 1945 I worked for the
                    U. S. Government.</p>
                <p>I am at complete loss why I am not permitted to return; all the more since I
                    never acquired any other nationality. I entered the <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__684" type="place">USA</rs> on a visitor&apos;s visa
                    when I came from <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__738" type="place">China</rs> in
                    1940, and I always made it clear to the immigration authorities here that I had
                    the intention to return to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place"
                        >Germany</rs> as soon as <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__910" type="person"
                        >Hitler</rs> was defeated.</p>
                <p>What would you suggest for me to do? Do you know anybody in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__554" type="place">Washington</rs> to whom I could
                    present my case with some hope of success?</p>
                <closer><salute>With kind personal regards,</salute><signed>Yours, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__115" type="person">H. W.
                        Baerensprung</rs></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
